2026-08-18T22:20:15.9722627Z > # These are statistical-validation suites -- bivariate association sandwiches,
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9723797Z > # the G4/G5 missing-response foundation, zero-one-beta, bivariate Gaussian, and
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9724344Z > # the profile-target matrix -- not "does the package install and work" tests.
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9724847Z > # They still run in full in repository CI, where NOT_CRAN=true. Nothing is
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9725320Z > # deleted and no test is weakened; this only changes which lane runs them.
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9725673Z > #
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9725957Z > # The patterns are ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored "zero-one-beta" also
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9726456Z > # matches test-missing-predictor-zero-one-beta.R, and an unanchored
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9726982Z > # "biv-gaussian" also matches test-missing-response-biv-gaussian.R -- neither is
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9727493Z > # intended, and both must keep running on the CRAN lane.
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9727807Z > #
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9728129Z > # `^julia` excludes every test-julia-*.R file. That alone is NOT enough: CRAN-lane
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9728647Z > # files such as test-binomial-response.R still call engine = "julia" inside
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9729157Z > # expect_error(), and Workflow G now admits fixed-effect binomial into the Julia
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9729889Z > # bridge, so the call reaches JuliaCall::julia_setup() before any rejection.
2026-08-18T22:20:15.9731272Z > # Ligges win-builder (2026-08-16/17) hung there for ~10448s even after #1061.
